        <mxCell id="note1" value="Colors = layers (a layer only calls the one below it)&#10;Blue: HTTP. Routes, and app.py, which puts the parts together&#10;Purple: the shapes of requests, with their validation&#10;Green: the rules, and what they ask of others: user-service (who is asking),&#10;    book-service (take copies), the bill layout, the mail server&#10;Yellow: storage (orders in MySQL or in memory, bill files on disk)&#10;Grey: start-up, settings, plain data&#10;Red: errors&#10;&#10;Python modules that hold functions rather than a class are drawn as &lt;&lt;module&gt;&gt;.&#10;Not drawn: every layer may raise the red errors; errors.py answers them in one place.&#10;Not drawn: bill.py and SmtpMailer read Order; bill.py reads RENT_RATE and RENT_DAYS.&#10;Not drawn, to keep lines from crossing: routes.py also calls ReportService, which reads&#10;the period's orders through OrderRepository.list_between; SalesReport also holds BestSellers." style="shape=note;size=14;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="740" y="1680" width="640" height="260" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
